WEBVTT

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:06.950
Dennis, these cheers are 
for both you and Kaito.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.920
Both of you, together,

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.860
brought smiles to all these people.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.980
It was a brilliant show!

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.460
Come with me...

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.870
I'm sure you can make 
even more people smile.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.610
You can change Academia!

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.240
I can't do that.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.550
I betrayed Yuya and Kurosaki.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.720
I can't return to them now.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:38.680
You...

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.350
Don't panic!

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.360
I'll tell you where Ruri is.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.390
And the girl named Rin, as well.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.590
Rin? The one Hugo's looking for?

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.430
They're at the top of the towers.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.960
Rin's at the top of Academia's east tower.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.800
Ruri's at the top of the west tower!

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.000
What are you...

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.580
Guys!

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:12.650
Any news?

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.460
Nothing here.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.120
Yeah, out of the question.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.890
No use! I didn't find anything, either!

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:22.010
There isn't any ship that will let us on?

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.450
Y-You're...

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:27.830
Serena!

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.220
I know a ship.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.040
Come with me.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.740
In a world split into four dimensions,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:42.320
four boys exist, all with the same face.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:45.320
Their dragons call to each other,

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.630
almost as if seeking one another.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:26.990
Duel Pirate Captain Solo

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.360
A ship... You mean this?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.930
Isn't that a pirate ship?

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.850
Could an anachronism like that even 
make it to Academia's island?

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:42.010
What'd you say, bucko?

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:45.580
P-Pirate!

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.870
This is Captain Solo, the ship's captain.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.890
It may look leaky, but it sails fine!

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.680
I guarantee it.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.350
Are you kidding me?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.630
Serena, I'm glad you're safe.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.820
I've been worried for so long.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.460
After he sent you back to Academia...

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:14.890
After I was sent back to Academia,

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:17.590
I waited for a chance to reunite with you.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:21.580
Then I received information 
that you had come

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:24.210
to the Fusion Dimension 
to infiltrate Academia.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.210
That's why I came running.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.180
I see.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.780
Leave the rest to me!

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:36.220
I already know where Rin and Ruri, the girls 
Hugo and Kurosaki are looking for, are.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.420
You did all that for us?

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.390
Thanks, Serena!

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:42.820
What's all this "thanks" business?

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.330
I'm a member of the Lancers!

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:49.160
Yeah! Well said!

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:51.300
The bonds between Lancers are strong!

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.590
An Academia helicopter!

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:02.700
They've finally come, eh?

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.920
They're after Serena and Yuzu!

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.750
Get them both to the back!

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.350
Now, hurry.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.690
This way! This way!

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.070
Give us that woman!

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.120
You think we'll hand her over if you ask?

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.080
That's right! The man Gongenzaka will—

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:24.970
Yuzu!

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.910
What are you doing, Serena? Let me go!

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.300
Let me go!

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:36.870
Yuzu!

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:38.810
Hold on...

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:42.150
I'm the one you'll be fighting.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.760
Captain...

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.960
All wrapped up!

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.320
Wh-What are you doing?

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.030
Sawatari! Gongenzaka!

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.720
Let us go... Let go!

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.500
Damn! You tricked us, you...

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:01.310
Serena!

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.480
Blame your own foolishness.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:04.800
Yuzu!

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.010
Hold it.

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:09.650
I told you, I'm the one you're fighting!

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:18.460
Serena... Why?

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.810
Serena here.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:27.030
I have Yuzu Hiiragi in custody.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:30.550
Serena, why? Why are you doing this?

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:34.580
I thought you were one of us.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:38.980
You said you were a member 
of the Lancers...

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.440
Damn, she tricked us!

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.960
The man Gongenzaka has never 
faced such humiliation.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.230
Damn!

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:53.640
I thought it was suspicious!

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.160
That stupid pirate captain!

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:58.870
This was all a trap to kidnap Yuzu?

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.960
So what if it was?

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.920
I'll take back Yuzu!

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.570
Take me to Academia!

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.440
Sorry, but give up.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.940
You'll never reach that island.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:09.640
What?

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:15.610
Because you'll lose to me on this ship, 
and get turned into a card!

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:18.100
I won't let that happen!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.990
Field Spell Crossover.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.010
Duel!

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.430
Then, I'll go first.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:32.200
I activate my spell card 
Polymerization from my hand,

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:37.570
to send Skull Mariner and Skull Knight #2 
to my graveyard and fuse them!

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:39.980
Ship of the demon world 
covered in red skulls...

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.590
Knight of skulls who hides in darkness.

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:46.640
Become one and awaken 
the legendary pirate king!

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:47.980
Fusion Summon!

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:55.670
Come out, Captain Lock!

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:03.680
All that trouble to Fusion Summon, 
for 0 attack points?

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.300
What's he plotting?

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:10.650
When Captain Lock is on the field,

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:16.860
neither player can Normal or Special 
Summon monsters from his hand.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:18.740
They can't set monsters, either.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:19.710
What?

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.840
Action Spell Power Gem.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:30.710
I increase Captain Lock's attack points by 800!

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:42.080
I forgot to mention one thing.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:46.190
When a monster with 1000 or more 
attack points is on the field,

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:48.440
Captain Lock is destroyed.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.200
What are you talking about?

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:53.160
You just made it impossible to 
summon monsters like that!

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.230
Calm down, Sawatari.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:57.850
Captain Lock is a monster on the field, too.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:02.140
Which means if I raise Captain Lock's 
attack points to 1000 or more,

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.890
its own effect will destroy it.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:07.480
Try it, if you can.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.520
I set one card and end my turn.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:12.420
My turn!

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:18.170
My hand is all monsters and traps.

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:21.530
In this situation, to increase 
Captain Lock's attack points...

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:24.410
I'll need Action Cards!

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:31.560
There's one!

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:34.690
Not so fast!

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:42.280
Action Spell Fire Gem.

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:45.580
I deal 600 points of damage to Yuya Sakaki.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:01.310
Take this.

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:06.990
Damn!

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:08.700
Okay.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:11.150
This...

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:13.930
An Action Card that deals damage to me!

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:17.520
Oh, did you get a bad draw?

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:19.210
Unlucky you!

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:24.520
I can only have one Action Card 
in my hand at a time.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.370
If I want to get a new one, I have to use this.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.890
Action Spell Cursed Gem!

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:33.960
I deal 600 damage to myself!

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.170
What's the matter?

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:50.500
You're going to destroy yourself before 
Captain Lock gets the chance!

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.670
Action Spell Fire Gem.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:57.640
I deal 600 points of damage to Yuya Sakaki.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:08.650
Yuya's life keeps getting shaved away!

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:11.480
It's do or die, now. Endure it, Yuya!

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:14.410
Yeah, I won't give up.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:15.910
Somewhere...

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:20.460
Somewhere, there must be an Action Card 
to increase a monster's attack points.

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:23.930
What's wrong, kiddo? Worn out already?

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.850
But he knows this ship's deck 
like the back of his hand.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:30.630
No matter where I go, he beats me there.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:33.770
The deck?

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.600
Okay... I'll just have to chance it!

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:44.000
Give up and end your turn already.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:46.950
No matter what you try, 
I'll beat you to the punch, and—

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:54.460
What?!

00:11:57.430 --> 00:11:59.420
What? Balancing on a tightrope!

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:03.400
He is an entertainment duelist 
on my level, after all!

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:04.840
Where...

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:06.370
Where?

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:10.810
There!

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.170
Damn...

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:14.230
Hard to starboard!

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:16.250
Hard to starboard!

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:25.560
Yuya!

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:40.570
Yuya!

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:43.040
Spread your ebony wings,

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:46.920
and strike the ground with 
the speed of lightning!

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.660
Synchro Summon!

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:54.290
Rain down, Assault Blackwing — 
Raikiri the Rain Shower!

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:01.520
This monster is...

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:03.560
Yuya!

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:07.400
Layra! Crow!

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.350
What a relief...

00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:11.830
Tsukikage?

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:17.110
Now! Jump down!

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.000
Allies, eh?

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:25.280
Oh!

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:30.720
I'm glad I made it in time.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:32.880
Thanks, you saved me.

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.360
But what are you doing here?

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:36.300
We can talk later!

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:38.340
Sora!

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:40.160
You're in the middle of a duel, right?

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:41.500
Boy!

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.870
End your turn already!

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:45.080
See?

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:49.510
I set one card and end my turn.

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:55.180
My turn. Draw!

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:59.580
I activate my Continuous Spell Battle at Sea.

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:03.890
When Water Attribute Monsters on 
my side of the field attack you,

00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:05.890
their battle damage is doubled!

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:16.220
I'll turn you into flotsam, 
along with your allies.

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:18.770
I attack your boat directly!

00:14:39.380 --> 00:14:40.410
Yuya!

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.060
You...

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:44.800
I now end my turn.

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:48.330
My turn!

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:51.740
2000-point penalty for entering the battle.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:03.550
I thought I recognized you. 
You're the traitor Sora Shiunin.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:05.820
It's been a while, Captain.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:08.450
I see you still like your cosplay.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.360
And you're still a mouthy brat!

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.960
Serena's back with Academia, you know.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:21.630
If you also return, you can talk things 
over with the Professor...

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:26.100
You're getting on my nerves, the way you talk.

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:30.350
I'll get Serena back!

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:32.580
After I beat you!

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:35.020
Hey, hang on a minute...

00:15:35.020 --> 00:15:38.330
Do you even know Captain 
Lock's monster effect?

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.040
When Captain Lock is on the field,

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:46.700
neither player can Normal or Special 
Summon monsters from his hand.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:47.440
Right?

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:48.830
Th-That's right.

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:54.430
If you knew you couldn't summon, 
why did you join the battle?

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.800
You're just coming in to get beaten!

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:59.770
It's only my hand I can't summon from.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:05.240
Don't forget that I'm a Fusion user.

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:08.960
When I use the spell card 
Polymerization in my hand,

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:12.540
I can send two Fusion-component 
monsters to the graveyard,

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:16.230
to summon one Fusion Monster 
from my Extra Deck.

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:17.450
I get it.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:21.900
You can still summon if it's from the 
Extra Deck, rather than the hand.

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:27.230
Th-That's right! I was just testing 
to see if he understood.

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:32.630
I fuse Edge Imp Tomahawk and 
Fluffal Octopus in my hand!

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:36.960
Devil's claws and beast's fangs, 
become one in the whirlpool of mystery.

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:39.180
Show your new power and look!

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:41.180
Fusion Summon!

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:46.120
Appear, devil of the sea who grasps, 
and then sinks back into darkness,

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:48.490
Frightfur Kraken!

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:57.690
And in that instant, the appearance of a monster 
with 1000 or more attack points

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:01.030
causes Captain Lock to be 
destroyed by its own effect!

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.710
Don't think you've won yet!

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:13.110
I activate my Continuous Trap Perished Pirate!

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:18.150
I negate the effect of Captain 
Lock in my graveyard,

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:21.100
to Special Summon it in attack position!

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:32.000
Then, once per turn, I can select 
one monster in my graveyard,

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:36.600
and equip it to Captain Lock, adding its 
attack points to those of Captain Lock.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:40.230
I choose Skull Mariner!

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:51.200
And I activate my Action Spell Power Gem.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:55.140
I increase Captain Lock's attack points by 800.

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:10.900
My Captain Lock's attack points are now 
higher than those of your big octopus!

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:14.540
Now, try to attack! 
You'll just be hurting yourself!

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:18.210
I won't let you do it!

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:23.960
I activate my trap card Performapal Teamwork!

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:32.090
I can equip one Performapal, 
of 1000 or fewer attack points,

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.560
to a monster Special Summoned this turn.

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:40.550
I equip Performapal Sword 
Fish to Frightfur Kraken!

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:53.370
And Frightfur Kraken receives double 
Sword Fish's attack points!

00:18:56.150 --> 00:19:00.120
3400 attack points?

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.090
Nice assist!

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.290
Yeah!

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:09.460
I attack Captain Lock with Frightfur Kraken!

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:24.110
It isn't over yet.

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:29.880
Frightfur Kraken's monster effect 
allows it to attack twice per turn.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:31.650
What?!

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:36.820
Frightfur Kraken attacks Captain Solo directly!

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:59.840
So long, Captain!

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:01.710
Don't let them get away...

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:03.310
Hard to starboard!

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:07.340
Tsukikage, is that...

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:10.250
Yes, I borrowed it on the way.

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:19.280
Hey, do something!

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:20.860
It's no use, Captain!

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:23.870
I'll get you for this!

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:34.440
After you disappeared from 
the Synchro Dimension,

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:37.000
the Public Order Bureau was dissolved.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.780
And the running of City 
was left to the citizens.

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:44.300
It will probably be reborn into a place of 
equality, without Tops or Commons.

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:49.260
I see... I'm glad.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:54.240
We intended to help with 
City's restoration, too.

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:57.230
But Shinji and Mr. Tokumatsu told us to go.

00:20:57.800 --> 00:21:00.700
They said, "Leave this to us, and go."

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:04.340
That the Lancers have their own mission.

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.410
The Lancers...

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.750
Our own mission...

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.190
I'll get Yuzu back!

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:13.210
And Serena, too.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.190
Serena...

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:20.700
I don't think Serena kidnapped 
Yuzu of her own free will.

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:23.060
Serena's fought alongside us.

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:25.560
I'm sure there's a reason.

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:28.470
Yeah. I think you're right.

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:31.720
I've heard that the Professor

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:36.680
has someone who can get 
people to do what he wants.

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.260
Really?

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:39.380
Then, Serena is...

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:42.850
And Yuzu might end up the same way.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:45.320
Let's go to Academia.

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:48.780
We'll get Serena and Yuzu Hiiragi back,

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:52.790
crush Leo Akaba's ambitions, 
and end all of this.

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:55.260
We, the Lancers, will do it ourselves!

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:53.130
I am Diana, guardian of the west tower.

00:23:53.130 --> 00:23:56.350
You cannot proceed unless you beat me!

00:23:56.350 --> 00:23:58.000
Ruri is in here.

00:23:58.000 --> 00:23:59.750
Then, I'll crush you!

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:03.020
I am Apollo, guardian of the east tower.

00:24:03.020 --> 00:24:07.060
I have no use for an old man 
like you! Return Rin!

00:24:07.060 --> 00:24:10.590
If you want her back, you must beat me.

00:24:10.970 --> 00:24:15.150
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Guardians of the Sun and Moon.

00:24:15.150 --> 00:24:17.240
The fun is only getting started!
